# Shell scripts and the systemd unit MUST keep LF endings.
#
# This repository is partly authored on Windows, where the default checkout
# converts to CRLF. A shell script with CRLF fails on Linux as
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" - a message that says nothing about
# line endings and sends people looking for a missing interpreter.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
